{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584235-weird-places-to-find-inspiration-captain-america-winter-soldier-slash","id":584235,"title":"Weird Places to Find Inspiration: Captain America/Winter Soldier Slash","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-08T22:47:48-07:00","id":584235,"title":"Weird Places to Find Inspiration: Captain America/Winter Soldier Slash","content":"Anyway, I consider myself a fanfic writer of moderate talent, and like most fan authors, I am a voracious reader of other fans.<br /> <br /> One day, when browsing An Archive Of Our Own, I happened across one of the multitude of Steve/Bucky romances, <a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/1871955/chapters/4031307\" target=\"_blank\">Out Of The Dead Land</a>, in which the Winter Soldier turns up at Steve's door, remembering being Bucky perfectly well.<br /> <br /> Unlike other romances of this premise, though, this is simply the Soldier's talent as an actor. Memories don't return that quickly, and in fact he doesn't feel worthy of being Bucky. He's just latched on to Steve as a new handler, because HYDRA took away his capacity to have anything other than the mission, and since Steve wants his friend back...<br /> <br /> While it could have gone <i>so wrong, </i>the premise manages to not only avoid the potential creep factor (apart from the personal anguish of a man pretending to be a past that's been semi-permanently denied to him), but turn it into an amazing story of coping with post-traumatic stress and learning to deal with newfound free will, with a side plot in examining the mechanics of dehumanization and identity. Via robot dopplegangers, because this is a superhero fanfic.<br /> <br /> What I found for amazing inspiration for changeling is the Winter Soldier's relationship with Zola, the man who turned him into what he is. One of the big things about this fic is that Zola thinks that a human who has become a machine in mind has reached a sort of transcendent state, incapable of self-doubt or angst. Hence why he wants Bucky back; the Winter Soldier was proof-of-concept, an obedient and effective gear in the mechanism of HYDRA, and now that he's more than a robot Zola wants to prove he'd go back to being one if given the choice. Sounds an awful lot like a Keeper attempting to understand why his toy rebelled without actually emphasizing with the toy at all. And a man trying to discover who he used to be despite seemingly everything having been erased sounds like a uniquely Changeling story.<br /> <br /> So, what do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T00:38:37-07:00","id":584359,"title":"","content":"Well I read the title and came here out of pure curiosity.<br /> <br /> 0_0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}